From e5be6e54764c3472e7137d87a67da722e54fc6a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Boyd <danieljboyd@icloud.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 13:12:34 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] cairo: print on a Windows printer device context

A printing bundle can now ask the cairo context for format
GSWin32PrinterFormat, with the printer's device context in the context
attributes, and the context draws through cairo's Windows printing
surface: GDI calls for the printer's own driver, rather than PostScript
that only PostScript printers read.  The surface scales the device
context to points with the origin at the paper's corner, and starts and
ends each page (StartPage, EndPage), which the context now tells its
surface about.
